                <pb facs="0733" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-16T09:00:00-04:00">August 16, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Felix Paivac [<hi rendition="#italic">Paiva</hi>], former Vice President and
                    recently professor of law, being sworn in as President 10 o’clock this morning.
                    Cabinet announcements expected shortly afterwards.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
